{"id":1771365,"retrievedAt":"2026-09-16T15:42:05.967Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[],"homepage":"","id":1771365,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_title":"Wiener Spaziergang","overview":"The first six images of Wiener Spaziergang (Viennese Stroll, 1965), for example, are ghoulishly amusing. Painted white, with a jagged slash painted through the middle of his body, Brus takes a walk through Vienna’s historical centre. He is documented walking past smart storefronts and tourist hotspots, is gawped at by fussy locals, and finally booked and firmly rebuked by a stern-faced police officer. The later images are much more troubling. Lying prone, corpselike, on a table surrounded by scalpels, Brus claws at his sludge-covered face and appears to stab himself in the thigh. He eventually falls and drags himself, agonized, across the floor.","popularity":0,"poster_path":"/3IUGgneV24u2j2Ygc6g4eCU3NGQ.jpg","production_companies":[],"production_countries":[],"release_date":"1965-07-05","revenue":0,"runtime":2,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"Wiener Spaziergang","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"images":{"backdrops":[],"logos":[],"posters":[{"aspect_ratio":0.667,"height":3000,"iso_3166_1":null,"iso_639_1":null,"file_path":"/3IUGgneV24u2j2Ygc6g4eCU3NGQ.jpg","vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"width":2000}]},"external_ids":{"imdb_id":null,"wikidata_id":null,"facebook_id":null,"instagram_id":null,"twitter_id":null},"credits":{"cast":[{"adult":false,"gender":2,"id":1127099,"known_for_department":"Acting","name":"Günter Brus","original_name":"Günter Brus","popularity":0.5371,"profile_path":"/xksyEdp7UL3oCim5NyF18ay9B0O.jpg","cast_id":1,"character":"Himself","credit_id":"6aa9e2bb4ae11bdbee31d373","order":0}],"crew":[{"adult":false,"gender":0,"id":2067978,"known_for_department":"Acting","nam